WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.500
Pairing buddy is the person in the second chair.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.560
It sits beside you in Neovim,

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.119
and speaks up only when it matters.

00:00:08.119 --> 00:00:10.020
It never touches your files,

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.470
unless you hand it the wheel.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:13.930
A test is red,

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.470
and you start fixing the wrong file.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.370
Pair reads the code first,

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.630
then says it right under your line:

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.550
the cause is elsewhere.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.050
Alt J jumps there.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.900
Save, and it runs your tests.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.820
Your fix broke a queue test?

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.280
Pair says why, and Alt Y takes its fix.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.070
Or hand it the wheel with Pair drive.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.190
You watch it type, it tests your unsaved buffer,

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:43.360
and one undo takes it all away.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.060
Notes in the margin.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.840
A first slice from a blank page.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.520
A ledger of everything it did, and a morning pick-up.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.650
Any model, local or cloud.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:56.830
Pairing buddy:

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:58.730
the person in the second chair.
